~ start
Father: Qaswar!

Qaswar: Father.

Father: There you are. What kept you so long?

Qaswar: I'm sorry. I ran into some friends on the way back.
Qaswar: We started talking, and... I lost track of time.

Father: I see.
Father: But you know your mother must be worried sick by now.

Qaswar: I know, Father. I'm sorry.

Father: These are uneasy times, Qaswar.
Father: You cannot afford to wander about without telling us where you are.
Father: Next time, be more careful. Do you understand?

Qaswar: Yes, Father.

Father: Good.
Father: Now go. Your mother has been waiting for you.
Father: Let her know you're home safely.

Qaswar: I will, Father.

=> END
